{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler orchestrator pipeline) assigned task #5366: implement srd040-printenv requirements R2.2, R2.3, R2.4, and R3.1. This is a \"stitch\" task in a code generation pipeline for the go-unix-utils project. The specific requirements are:\n   - R2.2: Must exit 0 if all requested VARIABLE arguments are found in the environment\n   - R2.3: Must exit 1 if any requested VARIABLE argument is not found in the environment  \n   - R2.4: When no VARIABLE arguments are given, must always exit 0\n   - R3.1: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between Go binary and gprintenv reference binary\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/printenv/main.go` and `cmd/printenv/printenv_test.go`\n   \n   Acceptance criteria: compilation passes, go vet passes, differential tests for R2.2/R2.3/R2.4/R3.1 pass, and all previous tests (R1.1/R1.2/R1.3/R2.1) continue to pass.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: Go binary vs GNU reference binary (gprintenv) via pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - DiffTest struct with Name, Args, Stdin, Env, ExitCode fields\n   - Exit code semantics: 0 for success, 1 for missing variables, 2 for invalid options\n   - NUL-delimited output via -0/--null flag\n   - Copyright header must use SPDX format: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` / `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - No git commands allowed - orchestrator manages git externally\n   - Must write all code before building/testing\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd040-printenv.yaml`\n      - Defines the full SRD for printenv; only R2.2, R2.3, R2.4, R3.1 are in scope for this task\n      - Key: R3.2 lists required test coverage areas; R3.3 requires verifying no stderr for missing vars\n   \n   - `cmd/printenv/main.go` (existing, 77 lines)\n      - Already implements exit code logic for R2.2/R2.3/R2.4\n      - Has old copyright header (2024 format, not SPDX)\n      - Full existing code:\n      ```go\n      // Copyright 2024 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n      // Use of this source code is governed by a MIT-style\n      // license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n      \n      package main\n      \n      import (\n          \"fmt\"\n          \"os\"\n          \"strings\"\n          \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n      )\n      \n      func main() {\n          sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n          nullTerminate := false\n          args := os.Args[1:]\n          var positional []string\n          for i := range len(args) {\n              a := args[i]\n              if a == \"--\" {\n                  positional = append(positional, args[i+1:]...)\n                  break\n              }\n              if a == \"--null\" { nullTerminate = true; continue }\n              if a == \"--help\" { /* prints help, exits 0 */ }\n              if a == \"--version\" { /* prints version, exits 0 */ }\n              if strings.HasPrefix(a, \"-\") && a != \"-\" {\n                  for _, ch := range a[1:] {\n                      switch ch {\n                      case '0': nullTerminate = true\n                      default: fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"printenv: invalid option -- '%c'\\n\", ch); os.Exit(2)\n                      }\n                  }\n                  continue\n              }\n              positional = append(positional, a)\n          }\n          terminator := \"\\n\"\n          if nullTerminate { terminator = \"\\x00\" }\n          if len(positional) == 0 {\n              for _, e := range os.Environ() {\n                  fmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"%s%s\", e, terminator)\n              }\n              os.Exit(0)  // R2.4\n          }\n          exitCode := 0  // R2.2\n          for _, name := range positional {\n              val, ok := os.LookupEnv(name)\n              if ok {\n                  fmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"%s%s\", val, terminator)\n              } else {\n                  exitCode = 1  // R2.3\n              }\n          }\n          os.Exit(exitCode)\n      }\n      ```\n\n   - `cmd/printenv/printenv_test.go` (existing, 64 lines)\n      - Has differential tests covering: no args, single var, multiple vars, missing var (exit 1), mixed existing/missing (exit 1), null-terminated variants, long flag\n      - Has old copyright header\n      - Full existing code:\n      ```go\n      // Copyright 2024 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n      // Use of this source code is governed by a MIT-style\n      // license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n      \n      package main_test\n      \n      import (\n          \"os/exec\"\n          \"testing\"\n          \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n      )\n      \n      func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n          goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n          refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gprintenv\")\n          if err != nil { t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\") }\n          tests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n              {Name: \"no args full dump\"},\n              {Name: \"single existing variable\", Args: []string{\"HOME\"}},\n              {Name: \"multiple existing variables\", Args: []string{\"HOME\", \"PATH\"}},\n              {Name: \"missing variable\", Args: []string{\"NONEXISTENT_VAR_FOR_PRINTENV_TEST\"}, ExitCode: 1},\n              {Name: \"mix of existing and missing variables\", Args: []string{\"HOME\", \"NONEXISTENT_VAR_FOR_PRINTENV_TEST\"}, ExitCode: 1},\n              {Name: \"null terminated no args\", Args: []string{\"-0\"}},\n              {Name: \"null terminated single variable\", Args: []string{\"-0\", \"HOME\"}},\n              {Name: \"null terminated missing variable\", Args: []string{\"-0\", \"NONEXISTENT_VAR_FOR_PRINTENV_TEST\"}, ExitCode: 1},\n              {Name: \"long flag null\", Args: []string{\"--null\", \"HOME\"}},\n          }\n          testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n      }\n      ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - was interrupted after reading files, before implementing.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Analyzed existing code and determined that R2.2, R2.3, R2.4 exit code logic is already implemented in main.go\n   - Determined that R3.1 differential testing is already present in the test file\n   - Identified that additional test cases may be needed for completeness (e.g., verifying no stderr on missing variables per R3.3, or adding more explicit test names aligned with R2.2/R2.3/R2.4)\n   - Noted copyright headers need updating from 2024 to SPDX 2026 format\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - One massive message containing the full task specification including: role definition, repository file list, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), task details (#5366), execution constitution, go style constitution, constraints, description with requirements R1-R4 mapping to SRD R2.2/R2.3/R2.4/R3.1, shared protocols, and package contracts.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement/verify R2.2, R2.3, R2.4, R3.1 in cmd/printenv/main.go (may need copyright header update, minor code changes)\n   - Add/update test cases in cmd/printenv/printenv_test.go for full coverage of R2.2/R2.3/R2.4/R3.1\n   - Build with `go build -o bin/printenv ./cmd/printenv/`\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/printenv/...`\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/printenv/... -count=1` to verify all tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (SRD, main.go, test file) and was about to plan and implement changes. The existing code appears to already implement t